# Line endings are repo policy, not per-host config. Everything is committed and
# checked out LF on every OS, so the object database never depends on whether a
# contributor's core.autocrlf happened to be true, input, or false.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Content-addressed JSON: LF is pinned explicitly rather than inherited, so the
# rule survives someone later relaxing the wildcard above. text (not -text) keeps
# these hand-written, pretty-printed fixtures reviewable as diffs in a PR.
*.json text eol=lf
